ersible  so in this moment gabby no longer really  cares about inheriting the armored titan  her main goal is getting revenge which  again is one of the ways she mirrors a  young vengeful eren  unlike gabby falco's brainwashing from  mali has been slightly undone thanks to  the words of mr jaeger  as he understands that aliens from  parodies are retaliating for what was  done to them  and that all aliens are the same  regardless of whether they're born in  mali or if they're born in parodies  it caused ryan to have a mental  breakdown when he came to that same  realization  so kudos to falco for not freaking out  more scouts begin to board the airship  during the escape  but when loboth and gabby come face to  face he hesitates to shoot her because  she's a child  just like how sasha chose not to take  the shot against gabby as well  that's two times now that gabby's life  has been spared by someone who she then  went on to kill  as gabby gets her first kill of the  episode it provided a unique opportunity  because lobos odm gear was still  tethered to the airship gabby knew that  going onto this ship would be a suicide  mission  but she is willing to die to get that  revenge colt appears just before gabby  pulls the trigger  and the last time we saw him he said he  was going to look for falco having  finally found his younger brother  colt could only watch on in horror as  falco risked his life for gabby again  by zipping onto the airship alongside  her if falco was my younger brother i  would honestly be so sick of this crap  like this is the third time that we know  of where he's intentionally done  something like this  his actions were spurred on by what  reiner said to him about protecting  gabby  although given falco's track record i'm  sure he still would have done this exact  same thing  even if rainer didn't say that once they  made it onto the airship  gabby quickly takes aim at sasha and  gets her revenge by shooting her with  the rifle  there's a few things we need to unpack  here regarding gabby and sasha's brief  history so let's just start from the  beginning  during dinner in the braun household  reiner was asked by gabby's father about  the devils on the island  and the first person ryan mentioned to  his family was the girl who ate a potato  during the entrance ceremony  gabby was listening the whole time but i  don't think even she imagined that she'd  be killing these people so soon  a few episodes later gabby and sasha  made eye contact after sasha killed the  malian security guards  and we know for a fact that gaby liked  these guys because they cared for her  safety even though she was an aldian  this headshot from sasha was the final  straw that turned gabby into an  unstoppable force for revenge  and i find it ironic that sasha was  killed with a weapon belonging to the  man that she killed herself  as a member of the 104th cadet corps  potato girl was a character that we've  known since the early days of the series  and we saw she grew from a quirky and  occasionally mistakeful character  into one of the bravest and most  reliable soldiers that the scouts have  one thing that never changed about her  even during this episode was her  relentless obsession with food  so it's pretty fitting that her last  word was just meat  as everyone was just reacting to sasha  getting shot gabby and jean immediately  tried to kill each other  and they probably would have both died  if falco didn't intervene  the kids then get beat up by a group of  soldiers and i felt sorry for falco in  this scene because he really didn't do  anything  but yeah gabby definitely deserved it  sasha was slowly beating  out as connie tried to keep her awake  and this is even more heart-wrenching  when you remember  that sashi is basically the closest  thing he has to family i mean his mother  is technically alive although she is a  pure titan  but the rest of his family are all gone  so losing sasha is almost like losing a  sister to hi