ent of the survey core  since the beginning of the season it's  been obvious that the alien race is  growing more and more at risk  as the power of the titans is beginning  to become more irrelevant  when titans truly become useless then so  will the aliens themselves  and it's possible they could suffer more  than they currently do whatever zeke and  aaron have planned their goal would be  to reduce the suffering of aldians one  way or another  and this is possible now that they have  the founding titan and a titan of royal  blood  the last time both those elements were  in one place aaron was able to use the  full power of the founding titan  which also gives him the ability to  destroy the world with the wall titans  by having that power the island safety  should be guaranteed to an extent  because i mean who is going to come and  invade when you have the power to  destroy the world  anyway like i said in the intro zeke's  betrayal of mali has been subtly hinted  at throughout the season  with my favorite example being during  episode 4. in that episode  falco noticed that aaron had a baseball  glove and a baseball and asked him if  his family sent it to him  back in season 3 there was an episode  titled perfect game  with the title itself being a reference  to baseball terminology  during perfect game the beast titan held  rocks at the scouts several times  making baseball references throughout  and this kind of implied that zeke was a  fan of the sport  aaron having this gear subtly showed us  that zeke was the family member that he  was referring to and it was a clue that  they were now working together  another hint at zeke's portrayal  happened during the battle in liberio  in which he straight up says eren yeager  is not my enemy  even though it seemed like he was saying  it in jest we can now see that he  literally meant what he said  and peak's expression tells us that she  was probably suspecting something as  well  although to be fair porko also was kind  of shocked he also gave away his true  motives when he said that levi was  running out of time  as this was referring to the escape plan  they had in place we saw how levi was  checking his stopwatch  so basically zeke was reminding him  almost that you know you need to attack  me soon or else i won't be able to  escape  the plan to betray marley was set into  motion from episode 2  as zeke pushed the agenda to invade  parodies island it was because of this  suggestion  that the festival was later held in  liberia to declare war providing aaron  with the perfect battleground to do what  he needed to do  and for the scouts to swoop in and take  zeke to the island the plan was that  elena would take the draw and cart titan  out of the battle  hence why zeke didn't go with them as  they got trapped because those two  escaped  zika could pretend like he was genuinely  trying to kill the scouts  hence why he threw more rocks than he  was supposed to also if you're wondering  how he survived this attack from levi  it's because the captain sliced off his  limbs and then quickly pulled away his  body during the explosion i had so many  people asking me if levi committed  suicide in this moment  because when the way he kind of appears  in the anime you see the explosion but  you don't see levi get away  and i think the reason we didn't see  levi is because he would have been  holding zeke's body that would have  given away the surprise a bit too early  so i think  that's the reason why we didn't see  going back to sasha's death  the reaction of armin and mikasa was a  great depiction of genuine grief  which is something that attack on titan  has always done really well jon points  out that sasha's death was a direct  consequence of aaron going rogue by  himself  and whilst aaron is clearly hurt by this  he lets out a pain laugh  at hearing her final words the word meat  reminded him of that funny memory from  before the battle of trust  when sasha essentially risked getting  locked up by stealing meat from the  office's pantry  it was a wholesome memory that was  pretty much just classic sasha  and i feel that aaron really didn't know  how to react especially knowing that he  is responsible for what happened  the look on his face reminded me of that  timey kiss his story at hand just  straight up pain  with that said that was my review of  episode 8 of attack on titan season 4  which was honestly a roller coaster of  an episode as usual i'd appreciate if  you dropped a like if you like this  video  and share it with anyone who you think  might enjoy it thanks for watching as  always and until the next one  peace out

